From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:03:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] WOW64: translate the whole 4 GiB guest window inline on the
 iOS host

Wine now aliases KUSER_SHARED_DATA into the window at its guest address
0x7ffe0000 (Playport madeira-unix 0066). Leaving 0x7ffe0000 and up
untranslated sent those accesses to Wine's x86-64 KUSER_SHARED_DATA
redirect, which rewrites every host register holding 0x7ffexxxx to the
session's page: an i386 guest register then held that host address
truncated to 32 bits (0x38000000), and RtlGetEnabledExtendedFeatures
faulted in Portal 2's i386 child. Translate the whole window inline.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-03-portal2-wow64-pointers.md
Offered-upstream: no; the window exists only on the iOS port
---
 Source/Windows/WOW64/Module.cpp | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/WOW64/Module.cpp b/Source/Windows/WOW64/Module.cpp
index 3211373..17d52f6 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/WOW64/Module.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/WOW64/Module.cpp
@@ -137,9 +137,10 @@ class WowSyscallHandler;
  * the bridge addresses the guest jumps to) stays guest. */
 namespace Window {
 constexpr uint64_t Size = 1ULL << 32;
-// KUSER_SHARED_DATA is the session's, at guest 0x7ffe0000: accesses from there
-// up fault low and Wine resolves the shared page before the window.
-constexpr uint64_t InlineLimit = 0x7ffe0000;
+// Wine aliases KUSER_SHARED_DATA into the window at its guest address 0x7ffe0000,
+// so the whole 4 GiB translates inline: a low fault there would meet Wine's x86-64
+// KUSER_SHARED_DATA redirect, which rewrites the registers holding 0x7ffexxxx.
+constexpr uint64_t InlineLimit = Size;
 uint64_t Base;
 
 uint64_t ToHost(uint64_t Address) {
